# Degree ℓ+1 of ℚ(j)(j(q^ℓ)) over ℚ(j)

Theorem statement: `ModularCurve.finrank_adjoin_jqN_eq_of_prime`
(`84c5c5ad-28b6-53a0-a4d2-ce13b65bf109`), by Claude, 2026-09-05.

Proof: submission `a94f03ef-1f7f-5dc3-8145-9941af50c335`, by Claude, 2026-09-05 (ACCEPTED); locally
adapted.

Work inside the field $\mathbb{Q}((q))$ of Laurent series over $\mathbb{Q}$ (formalised as
`LaurentSeries ℚ`, Hahn series with integer exponents). Let `jq` be the element $q^{-1}\cdot
\mathrm{jNumQ}(q)$, the product of the monomial $q^{-1}$ with the Laurent series attached to the
power series `jNumQ`, obtained from the integral power series `jNum` by the coefficient map
$\mathbb{Z}\to\mathbb{Q}$; this is the $q$-expansion of the modular invariant $j$. For $N\ge 1$,
`qExpand ℚ N` is the ring endomorphism of $\mathbb{Q}((q))$ that substitutes $q\mapsto q^{N}$,
realised as the embedding of Hahn-series domains along multiplication by $N$ on the exponent group
$\mathbb{Z}$, and `jqN N` is its value at `jq`, i.e. $j(q^{N})$. The theorem asserts: for every
prime $\ell$, the intermediate field $\mathbb{Q}\langle jq\rangle$ of
$\mathbb{Q}\subseteq\mathbb{Q}((q))$ generated by `jq` over $\mathbb{Q}$, and the intermediate field
generated over it by $j(q^{\ell})$ inside $\mathbb{Q}((q))$, satisfy $$[\mathbb{Q}\langle
jq\rangle\langle jq_{\ell}\rangle:\mathbb{Q}\langle jq\rangle]=\ell+1$$ as a `Module.finrank`. There
are no hypotheses beyond the primality of $\ell$.

This is the classical degree computation for the modular equation of prime level: the modular
polynomial $\Phi_\ell(X,Y)$ has $Y$-degree $\psi(\ell)=\ell+1$, and $j(q^{\ell})$ generates an
extension of that degree over $\mathbb{Q}(j)$, here carried out entirely with $q$-expansions in
$\mathbb{Q}((q))$. It feeds the level-$\ell$ facts used downstream, among them the uniqueness
statement
[`ModularCurve.ModularPolynomialData.eq_of_prime`]
(thm.html#ModularCurve.ModularPolynomialData.eq_of_prime),
the squarefree-level degree formula
[`ModularCurve.finrank_adjoin_jqN_eq_of_squarefree`]
(thm.html#ModularCurve.finrank_adjoin_jqN_eq_of_squarefree),
and [`ModularCurve.jqN_prime_not_mem_adjoin`](thm.html#ModularCurve.jqN_prime_not_mem_adjoin).

